{"_id": "37870976|None", "id": "37870976", "infons": {}, "passages": [{"infons": {"journal": "N Engl J Med;2023Oct21. doi:10.1056/NEJMoa2306441", "year": "2023", "type": "title", "authors": "Zhou C, Tang KJ, Cho BC, Liu B, Paz-Ares L, Cheng S, Kitazono S, Thiagarajan M, Goldman JW, Sabari JK, Sanborn RE, Mansfield AS, Hung JY, Boyer M, Popat S, Mour&#xe3;o Dias J, Felip E, Majem M, Gumus M, Kim SW, Ono A, Xie J, Bhattacharya A, Agrawal T, Shreeve SM, Knoblauch RE, Park K, Girard N, PAPILLON Investigators, "}, "offset": 0, "text": "Amivantamab plus Chemotherapy in NSCLC with EGFR Exon 20 Insertions.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "3", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:C000718215", "type": "Chemical", "valid": true, "normalized": ["C000718215"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "C000718215", "biotype": "chemical", "name": "amivantamab", "accession": "@CHEMICAL_amivantamab"}, "text": "Amivantamab", "locations": [{"offset": 0, "length": 11}]}, {"id": "4", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D002289", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D002289"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D002289", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Carcinoma Non-Small-Cell Lung", "accession": "@DISEASE_Carcinoma_Non_Small_Cell_Lung"}, "text": "NSCLC", "locations": [{"offset": 33, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "5", "infons": {"identifier": "1956", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "74545", "valid": true, "normalized": [1956], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1956, "biotype": "gene", "name": "EGFR", "accession": "@GENE_EGFR"}, "text": "EGFR", "locations": [{"offset": 44, "length": 4}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"type": "abstract"}, "offset": 69, "text": "BACKGROUND: Amivantamab has been approved for the treatment of patients with advanced non-small-cell lung cancer (NSCLC) with epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) exon 20 insertions who have had disease progression during or after platinum-based chemotherapy. Phase 1 data showed the safety and antitumor activity of amivantamab plus carboplatin-pemetrexed (chemotherapy). Additional data on this combination therapy are needed. METHODS: In this phase 3, international, randomized trial, we assigned in a 1:1 ratio patients with advanced NSCLC with EGFR exon 20 insertions who had not received previous systemic therapy to receive intravenous amivantamab plus chemotherapy (amivantamab-chemotherapy) or chemotherapy alone. The primary outcome was progression-free survival according to blinded independent central review. Patients in the chemotherapy group who had disease progression were allowed to cross over to receive amivantamab monotherapy. RESULTS: A total of 308 patients underwent randomization (153 to receive amivantamab-chemotherapy and 155 to receive chemotherapy alone). Progression-free survival was significantly longer in the amivantamab-chemotherapy group than in the chemotherapy group (median, 11.4 months and 6.7 months, respectively; hazard ratio for disease progression or death, 0.40; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.30 to 0.53; P<0.001). At 18 months, progression-free survival was reported in 31% of the patients in the amivantamab-chemotherapy group and in 3% in the chemotherapy group; a complete or partial response at data cutoff was reported in 73% and 47%, respectively (rate ratio, 1.50; 95% CI, 1.32 to 1.68; P<0.001). In the interim overall survival analysis (33% maturity), the hazard ratio for death for amivantamab-chemotherapy as compared with chemotherapy was 0.67 (95% CI, 0.42 to 1.09; P = 0.11). The predominant adverse events associated with amivantamab-chemotherapy were reversible hematologic and EGFR-related toxic effects; 7% of patients discontinued amivantamab owing to adverse reactions. CONCLUSIONS: The use of amivantamab-chemotherapy resulted in superior efficacy as compared with chemotherapy alone as first-line treatment of patients with advanced NSCLC with EGFR exon 20 insertions. (Funded by Janssen Research and Development; PAPILLON ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT04538664.).", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "31", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:C000718215", "type": "Chemical", "valid": true, "normalized": ["C000718215"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "C000718215", "biotype": "chemical", "name": "amivantamab", "accession": "@CHEMICAL_amivantamab"}, "text": "Amivantamab", "locations": [{"offset": 81, "length": 11}]}, {"id": "32", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D002289", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D002289"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D002289", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Carcinoma Non-Small-Cell Lung", "accession": "@DISEASE_Carcinoma_Non_Small_Cell_Lung"}, "text": "non-small-cell lung cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 155, "length": 26}]}, {"id": "33", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D002289", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D002289"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D002289", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Carcinoma Non-Small-Cell Lung", "accession": "@DISEASE_Carcinoma_Non_Small_Cell_Lung"}, "text": "NSCLC", "locations": [{"offset": 183, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "34", "infons": {"identifier": "1956", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "74545", "valid": true, "normalized": [1956], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1956, "biotype": "gene", "name": "EGFR", "accession": "@GENE_EGFR"}, "text": "epidermal growth factor receptor", "locations": [{"offset": 195, "length": 32}]}, {"id": "35", "infons": {"identifier": "1956", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "74545", "valid": true, "normalized": [1956], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1956, "biotype": "gene", "name": "EGFR", "accession": "@GENE_EGFR"}, "text": "EGFR", "locations": [{"offset": 229, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "36", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D010984", "type": "Chemical", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D010984"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D010984", "biotype": "chemical", "name": "Platinum", "accession": "@CHEMICAL_Platinum"}, "t